Subject: amd_adl: keep ADL's types, entry points and GFX activity read that hex-gpu calls, add VRAM usage, memory and versions
Why: hex-gpu reads AMD GPUs on Windows through ADL (docs/design/gpu-telemetry.md G3): all-smi's ffi.rs is its transcription of AMD's ADL SDK headers and sensors.rs its PMLog sensor read. Kept: the context, adapter count, AdapterInfo (Windows layout, with its row sanity check and headroom array) and PMLog entry points and types, and the GFX activity sensor. Added from AMD's headers: ADL2_Adapter_VRAMUsage_Get, ADL2_Adapter_MemoryInfo2_Get with ADLMemoryInfo2, ADL2_Graphics_VersionsX2_Get with ADLVersionsInfoX2, and ADL_MAX_ADAPTERS, the bound on ADL's count. Removed: the temperature, power, fan and clock readings, Overdrive's capability call, the poison-fill row states and the tests, none of which hex-gpu reads. Layout assertions become compile-time array-length checks (Hex's clippy denies assert!), fields Hex never reads carry a leading underscore (rustc's dead-code lint), the activity is a typed refusal where the card publishes none or out of 0 to 100 rather than an Option (CLAUDE.md §3), and casts become checked conversions (CLAUDE.md §1).

